%N A399350 Array read by antidiagonals: T(n,k) is the number of independent vertex sets in the n X k projective plane graph.
%C A399350 The n X k projective plane graph is constructed from an n X k grid graph by adding edges connecting diagonally opposite vertices around the border of the grid. It is similar to the Moebius strip, but twists are in both horizontal and vertical directions.
%C A399350 Column 0 and row 0 are by convention only and were obtained by extrapolation of the row and column recurrences.
%C A399350 The graph contains a loop at the central vertex for n = 1 and odd k or odd n and k = 1.
%H A399350 Andrew Howroyd, <a href="/A399350/b399350.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..560</a> (first 33 antidiagonals).
%H A399350 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/IndependentVertexSet.html">Independent Vertex Set</a>.
%F A399350 T(n,k) = T(k,n).
